Z||000007||GT-maniac||11-29-2001||01:46 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Haze_Performance:<BR><B> This nose & side skirts were from them.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/015_15.JPG">   <P><BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I can't see those headlights being very usefull, kind of like those dinky little headlights on the first generation intrepids.<BR>Chrysler had a lot of complaints from intrepid owners and finally fixed the problem with the current generation. I can't fathom why people are constantly wanting to do away with the pop up lights anyway. I've never had a problem with them on either of my cars and it's not like the parts are that hard to find if they do break. The pop up lights make the fiero feel and look more like a sports car and not an econobox.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero005a.jpg">  <P>85 WS6 GT partly modified<BR>87 GT Loaded resto project<p>[This message has been edited by GT-maniac (edited 11-29-2001).]||||reg||1
