Z||000009||MinnGreenGT||11-29-2001||11:25 AM||||PISA corp ( <A HREF="http://www.cybercars.com/fierohq.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.cybercars.com/fierohq.html</A>  ) Also sells the 355 Nose in addition to the "Artero" nose (they do other body kits as well).<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cybercars.com/mnfr/fierohq/artfe1.jpg">  <P>Others have discussed using an Erebuni MR2 front end... but no one has spent the $500 to find out (that's a lot to spend on a part that might not fit!)<P>[EDIT]BTW: The only thing I don't like about most aftermarket fascias is the trim.  You lose the stock Fiero trim on the front of the car, but it remains the rest of the way around.  And my issue with the 355 nose (while it does look cool), is that the lines don't quite match.  The nose slopes a little more than the hood and does not have the "centerline" that the hood does. IMO[/EDIT]<P>------------------<BR>               <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GreenGT6.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by MinnGreenGT (edited 11-29-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000010||MinnGreenGT||11-29-2001||11:28 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by GT-maniac:<BR><B>  I can't see those headlights being very usefull...<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Actually many people really quite like the flush mount (<A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com/tom/" TARGET=_blank>Tom's</A>) headlight kit.  I recently acquired a set for my car (Not yet installed, but they have 100w HyperWhite bulbs) and I've heard from other owners that brightness/visibility is not an issue.<P>Here's a thread currently running about them: <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/012287.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/012287.html</A> <p>[This message has been edited by MinnGreenGT (edited 11-29-2001).]||||reg||1
