Z||000020||kempo||11-29-2001||03:35 PM||||About the front clips, 355 style noses, how well do they hold up in comparison to the normal ones?  Worth the price tag?  I am interested in obtaining one but have back and forth thoughts on what I want to do with my GT.  I love the look of it as most of you would agree.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_brow.gif">  As for the Artero, I think it's hideous!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif">  <P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.admist.net/gtsmall.jpg">    <BR>0-60 6.9 seconds||||reg||1
Z||000021||MinnGreenGT||11-29-2001||03:40 PM||||There is a difference in durability.  The stock Fiero fascias are produced from a highly flexible bumper-cover material.  You can tell by pressing on it that it's quite plyable.  The aftermarket stuff is produced from normal fiberglass, which is more rigid. Not completely solid, but almost.  This means that if you bump something with your Fiero fascia, you may induce some "spiderwebbing" or cracking of the paint.  Whereas with fiberglass, you risk cracking the material all the way through.  I don't think that the F355 nose sits as low to the ground as the stock GT fascia, so it is probably less likely to scrape or hit anything low (much like a coupe/formula front end).||||reg||1
